  "result": "Subcommands now get their own nested `default_map` entry. Before, they received the parent's entire map, so `runserver`'s `port` default was never found.\n\nThe cause was in `src/click/core.py` in `Context.__init__`. When a subcommand context inherited the map, it took `parent.default_map` whole. The documented format nests a subcommand's defaults under its name (`{\"runserver\": {\"port\": 5000}}`), so the lookup missed. The fix is one line, changed to `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`. A missing entry still yields `None`.\n\nVerification:\n- A reproduction with `default_map={\"runserver\": {\"port\": 5000}}` now prints `5000`. Before the fix it printed the parameter's default, `1`.\n- The full suite passes: 1906 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed.\n- I added `test_default_map_nested_for_subcommand` to `tests/test_defaults.py`. It fails without the fix and passes with it.\n\nI didn't add a `CHANGES.md` entry; say if you want one.",
